TASK: Add *Meta and *Shallow struct types to compose/rs/lib.rs for ALL entities that have a *Diff equivalent, and extend tests.

RULES:
- DO NOT create new files. Edit compose/rs/lib.rs directly.
- Follow the existing Rust patterns (derive Debug, Clone, Serialize, Deserialize, PartialEq, Default; use #[serde(rename_all = "camelCase")])
- Add Meta and Shallow types after each entity's Diff definition block

DEFINITIONS:
- **Meta** = entity WITHOUT any Vec<> fields AND without heavy properties (like blob in File). Same scalar fields only.
- **Shallow** = entity with Vec<> fields replaced by Meta item vectors. E.g. Kit.types: Vec<Type> becomes KitShallow.types: Vec<TypeMeta>.

### Sub-entity Meta structs to add:
- `AttributeMeta` = Attribute (no Vec fields)
- `PropMeta`: guid, quality (QualityId), value, unit — omit attributes
- `TagMeta`: guid, name, description, icon — omit attributes
- `ConceptMeta`: guid, name, description, icon — omit attributes
- `AuthorMeta`: guid, name, email — omit attributes
- `FileMeta`: guid, name, remote, folder, size, hash — omit blob, created_at, created_by, updated_at, updated_by stay
- `FolderMeta`: guid, name, parent, description — omit attributes, keep created/updated
- `QualityMeta`: omit benchmarks, attributes
- `PortMeta`: omit compatible_ports, attributes
- `ModelMeta`: guid, name, file, description — omit tags, attributes
- `ConnectorMeta`: guid, name, t, point, direction, description, port, mandatory — omit props, attributes
- `LayerMeta`: guid, path, is_hidden, is_locked, color, description — omit attributes
- `PieceMeta`: omit props, attributes
- `GroupMeta`: omit pieces (PieceId[]), attributes
- `ConnectionMeta`: guid, connected, connecting, gap, shift, rise, rotation, turn, tilt, u, v, description — omit attributes
- `StatMeta` = Stat (no Vec fields)

### Main entity Meta and Shallow:
**TypeMeta**: guid, name, parent, is_abstract, folder, stock, virtual_type, unit, location, icon, image, description, created_at, updated_at — omit models, connectors, props, attributes, authors, concepts

**TypeShallow**: All Type scalar fields + models: Vec<ModelMeta>, connectors: Vec<ConnectorMeta>, props: Vec<PropMeta>, attributes: Vec<AttributeMeta>, authors, concepts stay as-is (already IDs)

**DesignMeta**: guid, name, parent, is_abstract, folder, unit, can_scale, can_mirror, active_layer, location, icon, image, description, created_at, updated_at — omit pieces, connections, stats, props, layers, groups, attributes, authors, concepts

**DesignShallow**: All Design scalar fields + pieces: Vec<PieceMeta>, connections: Vec<ConnectionMeta>, stats: Vec<StatMeta>, props: Vec<PropMeta>, layers: Vec<LayerMeta>, groups: Vec<GroupMeta>, attributes: Vec<AttributeMeta>, authors and concepts stay

**KitMeta**: guid, name, version, remote, homepage, license, preview, icon, image, description, created_at, updated_at — omit types, designs, tags, concepts, ports, qualities, files, folders, authors, attributes

**KitShallow**: All Kit scalar fields + types: Vec<TypeMeta>, designs: Vec<DesignMeta>, tags: Vec<TagMeta>, concepts: Vec<ConceptMeta>, ports: Vec<PortMeta>, qualities: Vec<QualityMeta>, files: Vec<FileMeta>, folders: Vec<FolderMeta>, authors: Vec<AuthorMeta>, attributes: Vec<AttributeMeta>

